2a:T93f,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"n8n vs Zapier vs Make: which should I use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Zapier is simple for elementary 2-step tasks but becomes prohibitively expensive at scale. Make offers visual routing but retains usage tiers. n8n is the ultimate choice for technical teams and growing businesses: open-source, easily self-hosted, supports complex branching with custom JavaScript, and incurs zero per-execution costs while keeping all proprietary data on your private infrastructure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"n8n cloud vs self-hosted: what's the difference?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"n8n Cloud is a managed subscription hosted on n8n’s servers with monthly execution caps. Self-hosted n8n is installed on your private Linux server via Docker. Self-hosting grants total data privacy, eliminates task execution limits, enables direct database connections, and allows local AI models, costing only the base VPS fee (typically $10–$20/month)."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"n8n community vs enterprise edition: which do I need?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The n8n Community Edition is free, open-source, and includes all core nodes, AI agent tools, and webhook features needed by 95% of businesses. The Enterprise Edition adds SSO authentication, advanced role-based access control (RBAC), and external audit logs, which are primarily necessary for large corporate compliance teams."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do you ensure self-hosted n8n remains reliable and secure?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"I configure production n8n deployments with PostgreSQL (never fragile SQLite), automatic SSL certificates, Docker restart policies, and daily off-site database backups. I also configure webhook secret validation, environment-level credential encryption, and dedicated error-handling notification pipelines."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can n8n connect to my internal custom database or proprietary software?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Because n8n provides native PostgreSQL, MySQL, and MongoDB nodes alongside HTTP Request and Code nodes, I can connect it directly to your private databases, custom APIs, internal microservices, and private webhook endpoints behind your firewall."}}]}18:["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2a"}}]
